taxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 pdfomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 for saleomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 1omim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 partsomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 2omim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 10omim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 freeomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 3Mouse Genome Informaticshttps://www.informatics.jax.org › disease › 620208autosomal recessive spinocerebellar ataxia 33 Disease ... autosomal recessive spinocerebellar ataxia 33 (DOID:0070414) Alliance: disease page Synonyms: SCAR33 Alt IDs: OMIM:620208 Definition: An autosomal recessive cerebellar ataxia characterized by delayed motor development apparent in infancy, unsteady ataxic gait, intention tremor, nystagmus, and speech delay with dysarthria that has_material_basis_in homozygous mutation in the RNU12 gene on ... National Center for Biotechnology Informationhttps://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov › medgen › 1824070Spinocerebellar ataxia, autosomal recessive 33 (Concept Id ... Definition Autosomal recessive spinocerebellar ataxia-33 (SCAR33) is a neurologic disorder characterized by delayed motor development apparent in infancy, unsteady ataxic gait, intention tremor, nystagmus, and speech delay with dysarthria. Some patients have seizures and/or learning difficulties. Brain imaging shows cerebellar hypoplasia (Elsaid et al., 2017). [from OMIM] malacards.orghttps://www.malacards.org › card › spinocerebellar_ataxiaSpinocerebellar Ataxia, Autosomal Recessive 33 - MalaCards Autosomal recessive spinocerebellar ataxia-33 (SCAR33) is a neurologic cerebellar ataxia caused by homozygous mutation in the RNU12 gene on chromosome 22q13. It presents in infancy with delayed motor development and is characterized by unsteady ataxic gait, intention tremor, nystagmus, and speech delay with dysarthria. Genomics England PanelApphttps://panelapp.genomicsengland.co.uk › panels › 477Gene: RNU12 (Ataxia and cerebellar anomalies - narrow panel)Dec 19, 2025 ·   This gene is putatively linked to Spinocerebellar ataxia, autosomal recessive 33, MIM:620208 and linked to CDAGS syndrome, MIM:603116 (OMIM accessed 19th Dec 2025). OMIMhttps://www.omim.org › clinicalSynopsis › 620208SPINOCEREBELLAR ATAXIA, AUTOSOMAL RECESSIVE 33; SCAR33 - OMIM The full-text, referenced overviews in OMIM contain information on all known mendelian disorders and over 15,000 genes. OMIM focuses on the relationship between phenotype and genotype. It is updated daily, and the entries contain copious links to other genetics resources. OMIMhttps://www.omim.org › entry › 620204Entry - *620204 - RNA, U12 SMALL NUCLEAR; RNU12 - OMIMJul 6, 2023 ·   Spinocerebellar Ataxia 33, Autosomal Recessive In 6 affected members of a consanguineous kindred from Qatar with autosomal recessive spinocerebellar ataxia-33 (SCAR33; 620208), Elsaid et al. (2017) identified a homozygous C-to-T transition at position 43,011,333 on chromosome 22, within the RNU12 gene (620204.0001). \n                    \n                \n            \n                        \n                        Searches related to OMIM 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 RNU12omim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 pdfomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 2omim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 1omim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 for saleomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 freeomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 10omim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 partsomim 620208 spinocerebellar ataxia autosomal recessive 33 rnu12 3\n                    \n                \n                People also search for        \n            \n        \n         